      "description": "Watch Grimsby vs Exeter City highlights and goals from League Two on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 15, 2026. A tense encounter in League Two On August 15, 2026, Grimsby faced off against Exeter City in a highly anticipated football clash. Both sides approached the match with caution, looking to establish control in a contest where every possession mattered. The breakthrough moment As the first half progressed, the deadlock was finally broken in the 36th minute. Charles Vernam provided a clinical assist, setting up Harvey Rodgers , who fired home to give his side the lead. This goal forced the game to open up, as the visitors scrambled to find a response before the referee blew for half-time. Tactical battles and final whistle Physicality played a key role throughout, with Jake Doyle-Hayes receiving a yellow card in the 23rd minute and Cameron McJannet booked shortly before the break. The second half saw both managers utilize their benches extensively. Tactical adjustments, such as the introduction of Jamie Walker for Kieran Green , defined the late stages of the game. Despite the pressure in the closing minutes, Grimsby held their ground, ultimately securing the victory when the final whistle sounded at 90+6 minutes."
